## Context

Replace the old merge-and-tombstone contract. Scope expansion preserves identity; a broader synthesis gets a new UUID and generalizes references; supersession is a separate explicit withdrawal decision.

Design baseline: v7. v6 was merged by PR #903 and is frozen at `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-v6.md`; v7 closes the acceptance review's four §12.1 conditions and settles the nomenclature, leaving the architecture and this ticket's scope unchanged. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`, `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-nomenclature.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Dreaming skill; manually supplied proposals (optional automated discovery in 0912); library schema/admission; existing shared-change review process.

## Actions

1. Provide a reviewed editorial workflow that considers evidence, conditions, exceptions and usefulness, with no-change as a first-class result. Manual agent-led review suffices for the base; automated model-assisted generalisation is an optional strong-host extension, not a prerequisite for closure or harvesting.
2. Record accepted synthesis and its rationale with source revisions and reviewer identity; record model/prompt identity when a model is used. Retain particulars active unless an explicit independent supersession/retraction is justified.
3. Route shared semantic changes through the existing review process. Do not infer decision authority from recurrence or a model-authored field.
4. Compile accepted changes independently of pending proposals; protect against changed source revisions at integration.

## Test

Mechanical fixtures verify UUID/relationship/lifecycle invariants through the common mutation path. The base must be exercisable with recorded manual judgments and no model service. Behavioural cases cover genuine synthesis, lexical false positives, a repeated observation warranting no action and a useful local exception. Do not make guaranteed model judgment a deterministic gate.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v7, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Accepted generalisation retains sources and resolvable provenance.
- [ ] No occurrence threshold or straddling-tier rule automatically retires content.
- [ ] Conflicting edits are reported; no unreviewed shared semantic change lands.
